Z||000000||fierobob88||11-27-2001||07:26 PM||||sup guys...I have a 4 cylindar, and found some dyno numbers from a website on the motor.  I was suprised to see how well the car responded to the mods that it had, was curious if anyone has any of these mods on their 4 bangers, and how well they do work?  Here are the charts<BR>Stock motor.<BR>96 hp @ 4000 rpm & 136 ft. lbs. of torque @ 3000 rpm. <BR>Stock motor with just headers.<BR>113 hp @ 4000 rpm & 153 ft. lbs. of torque @ 3500 rpm <BR>Stock motor with header and ported heads.<BR>132 hp @ 5000 rpm & 159 ft. lbs. of torque @ 3500-4000 rpm. <BR>Stock motor with just Lunati cam.<BR>139 hp @ 5500 rpm & 143 ft. lbs. of torque @ 4500 rpm. <BR>Lunati cam with headers and nothing else.<BR>164 hp @ 5500 rpm & 167 ft. lbs. of torque @ 4500 rpm <BR>Lunati cam with headers & ported heads.<BR>192 hp @ 6500 rpm & 177 ft. lbs. of torque @ 5000 rpm with not bottom-end power. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ITB 2M4||11-27-2001||09:34 PM||||What website was this?  I've got a Headman header, a port-matched head, and a K&N filter.  It made 88hp at the rear wheels, and 110ft./lbs. of torque.  Granted, it's all stock internals (balanced and blueprinted), but I'd love to have 110hp at the rear wheels.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||11-27-2001||09:50 PM||||Someone was dreaming or just making up numbers.  That kind of horsepower is not possible with those modifications.  Be lucky to get 120 max...i'd say.  However if you're willing to spend alot of money for a new racing head.....and alot of money period you can attain those figures.||||reg||1
